      template_source: (
          #|# Repository Guidelines
          #|
          #|This is a MoonBit Proton native desktop app.
          #|
          #|## Commands
          #|
          #|- Format with `moon fmt`.
          #|- Check with `moon check --target js,native --diagnostic-limit 80`.
          #|- Run with `proton_cli dev` from the project root.
          #|- Build with `proton_cli build`.
          #|- Inspect packaging with `proton_cli package --dry-run`.
          #|- Package with `proton_cli package`.
          #|- If the Proton installation is missing, run `proton_cli cef setup`.
          #|
          #|## Project Notes
          #|
          #|- `shared/` contains the target-neutral typed application contract.
          #|- `frontend/` is a JavaScript Rabbita module owned by Warren.
          #|- `backend/` is a native Proton module.
          #|- `proton.project.json` is required by `proton_cli dev`, `build`, and `package`.
          #|- Keep command and event names in `shared/todo_contract.mbt`.
          #|- Bind shared commands explicitly in backend/todo/commands.mbt.
          #|- Write commands return business outcomes. Events invalidate snapshots; queries
          #|  use the application-local internal/query module. Keep request generations,
          #|  listener readiness, and invalidation coalescing out of the Todo model.
          #|- Do not reintroduce the old WebSocket app runtime route.
          #|
      ),
    },
    {
      output_path: "README.md",
      template_name: "isomorphic/README.md.mtpl",
      template_source: (
          #|# {{title}}
          #|
          #|An isomorphic MoonBit Todo app generated by `proton_cli new`.
          #|
          #|- `shared/` defines the typed commands, events, and payloads used on both sides.
          #|- `frontend/` is a Rabbita application built and served by Warren.
          #|- `backend/` owns the in-memory Todo state and runs the Proton desktop runtime.
          #|
          #|## Setup
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|moon update
          #|proton_cli cef setup
          #|```
          #|
          #|## Check
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|moon check --target js,native --diagnostic-limit 80
          #|```
          #|
          #|## Dev
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|proton_cli dev
          #|```
          #|
          #|`dev` reads the required `proton.project.json`, starts Warren in `frontend/`,
          #|waits for the development URL, then runs `backend/app`.
          #|
          #|## Build
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|proton_cli build
          #|```
          #|
          #|`build` runs Warren {{warren_version}} through `moonx` in `frontend/`, validates
          #|`frontend/dist`, and builds `backend/app` for the native target.
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|proton_cli build -- --release
          #|```
          #|
          #|## Package
          #|
          #|The top-level `identifier` is the application's canonical identity. The
          #|`package` block contains the remaining static packaging metadata:
          #|
          #|```json
          #|{
          #|  "identifier": "com.example.my-app",
          #|  "package": {
          #|    "product_name": "My App",
          #|    "version": "0.1.0",
          #|    "output": "dist"
          #|  }
          #|}
          #|```
          #|
          #|When `formats` is omitted, Proton selects the current host's default package
          #|formats. Use `package.platforms` for platform-specific formats, resources, or
          #|signing targets.
          #|
          #|Window behavior, the asset entry, single-instance handling, and renderer
          #|permissions are declared by the Proton `App` builder in `backend/app/main.mbt`.
          #|
          #|Inspect the resolved package plan, then create the current host's native
          #|artifacts:
          #|
          #|```sh
          #|proton_cli package --dry-run
          #|proton_cli package --release
          #|```
          #|
          #|## Layout
          #|
          #|- `shared/todo_contract.mbt` is the cross-target contract source of truth.
          #|- `frontend/main/main.mbt` handles Rabbita state, commands, and live events.
          #|- `backend/todo/` owns state and typed command handlers.
          #|- `backend/todo/commands.g.mbt` is generated from `commands.mbt` by the Moon
          #|  prebuild rule. Ordinary `moon check`, `build`, and `run` commands keep it
          #|  current through `moonx moonbit-community/proton_codegen`.
          #|- `backend/app/main.mbt` assembles and runs the application.
          #|- `dist/` contains packaged application artifacts.
          #|
          #|## Contract and state flow
          #|
          #|Commands are bound explicitly in backend/todo/commands.mbt; the application
          #|requires no code-generation build rule. Shared response enums distinguish
          #|business rejection from transport failures.
          #|
          #|Each ready window attaches its own event emitter and detaches it on close.
          #|Writes return a business result and notify those explicit destinations that
          #|the data changed. The application-local frontend/internal/query module owns
          #|listener-first initialization, cancellation, invalidation coalescing, and stale
          #|completion guards. The Todo model contains only its draft and business error.
          #|Input changes use set_input; refresh retries the read or a failed listener.
          #|Loading and failure retain previous data with its original query input. This
          #|module is an internal prototype, not a stable Proton API; see its README.
          #|
          #|Run the generated backend and frontend regression tests with:
          #|
          #|    moon -C backend test todo --target native
          #|    moon -C frontend test --target js
          #|
      ),
    },
